# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug
target

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/

# Internal architecture notes (see concepts/README.md), anchored to the repository root.
# ROADMAP.md is the spec of specs: every open item names its feature specification.
# `tests/concepts.rs` guards them and skips when the directory is absent, which is what CI sees.
#
# The third-party corpus — ITU-T recommendations, RFCs, IEC previews, Wireshark's ASN.1
# modules (GPL-2), the SCL XSD, sample captures and the OpenSCD fixtures — lives at
# `concepts/reference/` and is covered by this line: fetched by scripts/fetch-references.sh,
# indexed in `concepts/REFERENCES.md`, and never redistributed from here.
/concepts/
# Its predecessor: a single unlinked, unchecked design document, split into concepts/.
# Kept ignored so it cannot come back by accident.
CONCEPT.md

# This project's own feature specifications, and the Spec Kit machinery that produces them:
# one `specs/NNN-slug/` per ROADMAP item, `.specify/memory/constitution.md`, and the
# `/speckit-*` skills. Same rule as `concepts/` — internal, and the published tree may not
# cite a path its reader does not have; `cargo test --test concepts` fails on one that does.
# Matching eebus, iso15118, bergman and agentplane.
#
# Until 2026-11-09 `specs/` held the reference corpus now under `concepts/reference/`;
# a stale copy is ignored by the same line.
/specs/
/.specify/
/.claude/
.DS_Store

# Fuzzing corpora and working artifacts. `fuzz/regressions/` is deliberately *not* ignored:
# an input a fuzzer crashed on stops being an artifact once the bug is fixed and becomes the
# cheapest proof it stays fixed, so it is renamed after the bug, committed, and replayed by
# `tests/regressions.rs`.
/fuzz/target/
/fuzz/corpus/
/fuzz/artifacts/
/fuzz/Cargo.lock

# Zola build output
/site/public/
